reasoning_standard_meta_recipe
  record_type "meta_recipe"
  topic "reasoning_standard"
  title "The reasoning standard: how depth, refutation-first logic, formalized instructions and computed trust are produced as a formal procedure"
  summary "Machine-readable recipe for reproducing the reasoning standard of issue #1073 from data and pure predicates. The issue pointed at a reference dialog and asked for its depth to become the floor for every request, for reasoning to be refutation-first with a wide variety of refutations, for gathered internet instructions to be formalized into machine-checkable instruction sets, for official documentation to be a default step, and for source trust to be computed from primacy rather than assumed. Requirement 6 asked for all of it as formal checkable procedures, reachable with the language model removed. The recipe is grounded: tests/unit/specification/reasoning_standard_meta_algorithm.rs asserts the live source still matches every step, gate, function and pinning test listed here."
  generalization "Any reasoning requirement is turned into a gate by the same eight ordered steps. To add one: declare it in data/meta/reasoning-standard.lino with an order, a trigger naming what must be present in an episode for the gate to apply, a requirement in the standard's own words, and the slug it fails with; add whatever the gate reads to the episode record; write its evaluator as a pure predicate over that record in src/reasoning_standard/mod.rs; give it a threshold in the same data file if it compares against a number; and add the reference-episode mutation that must flip it. Nothing about the new gate is prose in a prompt, and nothing about it consults a model, a clock or the network."
step_declare_the_standard_as_data
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "1"
  id "declare_the_standard_as_data"
  title "Declare the standard as data, not as guidance"
  detail "data/meta/reasoning-standard.lino declares seven ordered gates and five numeric thresholds. Each gate carries a trigger, the requirement in words, the behaviour it was adopted from in the reference dialog, and the slug it fails with. standard() loads and validates it: contiguous orders, a known trigger, a non-empty requirement and failure slug, at least one threshold, and a depth floor that reads unconditional. A standard that fails to load is recorded as an error rather than skipped."
  seed_file "data/meta/reasoning-standard.lino"
step_record_the_episode
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "2"
  id "record_the_episode"
  title "Record one reasoning pass as an episode"
  detail "A ReasoningEpisode is the record every gate reads: the observations that were executed and what they printed, the claims that were made and which observations support them, the sources that were weighed, the instruction excerpts that were gathered, the refutations that were attempted, the actions that changed the world with their before and after measurements, and the conclusions. It round-trips through Links Notation, so an audit can be replayed from the record alone."
  seed_file "src/reasoning_standard/episode.rs"
step_derive_source_trust
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "3"
  id "derive_source_trust"
  title "Derive every source's trust from its primacy chain"
  detail "PrimacyChain::derive_trust computes a SourceTier from how far a source stands from the primary record and whether every hop names its upstream: a chain with no hops, an unfounded hop, or a repost derives Unoriginal; distance zero derives OriginalFirstParty, or OriginalJournalism when the hop is a first-hand record; distance one or more derives IndependentCorroboration. resolve_conflict prefers the source closer to the primary record and leaves an equal-distance conflict unresolved rather than picking a side."
  seed_file "src/reasoning_standard/trust.rs"
step_formalize_gathered_instructions
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "4"
  id "formalize_gathered_instructions"
  title "Compile gathered instructions into checkable steps"
  detail "formalize merges the steps several sources give for one task class into a single ordered instruction set, keyed by the action, unioning the checks and recording which sources gave each step. A step two sources give is corroborated; a step with no check is unverifiable and fails the gate, because prose that cannot be checked is not a formalized instruction."
  seed_file "src/reasoning_standard/instructions.rs"
step_attempt_varied_refutations
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "5"
  id "attempt_varied_refutations"
  title "Attempt varied refutations before leaning toward a conclusion"
  detail "RefutationLedger collects the probes aimed at one conclusion and counts variety two ways: how many distinct mechanisms were tried, and how many of the three kinds (a different mechanism, a different source, a different denied assumption) they span. The ledger is discharged only when every probe is settled by evidence; a probe that survived on evidence proves the alternative instead; an unchecked probe leaves the ledger open and carries the blocker that stopped it."
  seed_file "src/reasoning_standard/refutation.rs"
step_verify_after_acting
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "6"
  id "verify_after_acting"
  title "Re-measure after every change"
  detail "Every action that changed the world carries a measurement taken afterwards, backed by an observation of its own, so the effect is re-measured rather than assumed. This is the reference dialog's own habit of re-running the measurement after every deletion and quoting the new number, turned into a predicate."
  seed_file "src/reasoning_standard/episode.rs"
step_report_failures_honestly
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "7"
  id "report_failures_honestly"
  title "Report a partial result as partial, with its reason"
  detail "Action::is_honestly_reported requires the reported outcome to equal the real one and, when the action did not fully succeed, requires the reason to be named. Rounding a partial result up to a success fails the gate, which is the reference dialog's habit of reporting the leftovers it could not remove and saying why."
  seed_file "src/reasoning_standard/episode.rs"
step_audit_unconditionally
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "8"
  id "audit_unconditionally"
  title "Audit every request against every gate and record the ledger"
  detail "audit evaluates every declared gate on the episode and reports each one as satisfied, violated, or not triggered together with the trigger that was false — never omitting a gate, whatever the request looked like. record_meta_core calls it on every request through record_reasoning_standard, with no mode knob in front of it, so the depth floor cannot become conditional on difficulty or on being asked for. The verdict is confirmed, refuted, or the honest default: not confirmed and not refuted, carrying the blockers by name."
  seed_file "src/meta_core.rs"
